 ## 20. Lịch sử quyết định
 
+- **2026-11-24 — the borrow-vector module keeps its winpid read and drops its kill-wait copy.** `borrow_vectors.rs` backgrounds `sleep` under Git for Windows' `sh` and reads `/proc/$!/winpid` there, because only that shell can learn the Windows pid of its own background job; no Rust door can take the read over, so the file is an allowed entry (count 1) of the `process facts: read /proc` door, not debt. Its private `KILL_WAIT_MS` (2000) was a copy of `DEFAULT_KILL_WAIT_MS` in `port.rs` and now uses that constant; the module holds no `fence_lock` and no `TERM_WAIT_MS` (the fence state machine and its waits stay in `fence.rs`).
 - **2026-11-15 — `lock-status` and `lock fence` run in the host; the hot record and the beacon have one owner each.** (1) The hot record's reader and compare-and-clear are `hot_record.rs`; Node's functions call it and the writer stays Node until the Work state store moves (S7). Reused: `judge_here` of the process crate; `clearHotRecord` and the addon `hotRecordClear` binding were deleted when the fence moved, since nothing in Node cleans a record any more. (2) `lock-status` lists each row's instances by the registry's own path template (no table of lock files), and the host lists the three run-scoped layouts (workflow runs, assignment runs, open attempts) itself and passes them in, because the holder-lock crate may not know Execution layouts and the run supervisor already depends on it; the host twin is `apps/fgos/src/wiring/run_dirs.rs` with one fixture shared by the Node listers, and retires with the Execution port (S6a). (3) `lock fence` is `fence.rs`; without `--yes` it lists and refuses (`lock-fence-not-confirmed`, exit 2), on a terminal too (owner decision S23-Q3 = b); the terminal question is gone. A missing or unknown `lock` sub-command and a `--flag=value` spelling are refused as every host-served verb refuses them. (4) The beacon's record and vectors are the contract `main-checkout-activity.v1.json`, read by `status.rs` and by the commit gate's Node reader. Accepted differences from the Node verbs: a lock file whose registry placeholder is empty (`merge-slot--.lock`) is no instance; a refused signal names the holders already signalled; an unreadable beacon file answers the host's error text; `fence dispatch-cwd --param cwd=` on Windows (section 19). Evidence: the parity runs of the step against the base release (lock-status 29 cases, lock 35, git 25) and the owner tests named in the step's phase reports.
 - **2026-11-04 — documentation-cutover lease retired after the cutover landed; mechanism, verb, hook, lock row and doctor check removed.** The rank-10 `documentation-cutover` row, its band note and the section 19 lease contract are gone; the 2026-10-22 registration entry below stays as history.
 - **2026-10-22 — documentation lease registration, hardening lane:** Register `documentation-cutover` as a rank-10 repo lease, owner `documentation`, fence `none`, no legacy path, public acquire only; the main-ref sidecar owns persistent freeze and the kernel lock serializes transitions (sections 7 and 19).
