+
 - **2026-11-24 — The Node agent hook table and the Node shell-rc detector are deleted; Rust is the only owner of both (component-authority door rows `agent-hook-table`, `delete-guard-keyword-list` and `shell-rc-fgos-lines`).** `src/setup/agent-hooks.mjs` (last commit 871a77074) is gone: `packages/distribution/rust/src/agent_hooks.rs` is the one hook table and the one owner of the delete-guard prefilter keyword list, which it pins to `packages/distribution/contracts/delete-guard-prefilter.v1.json`. Workspace hook rows are installed through `fgos doctor --fix --only <fix-id>`, the door the live mailbox harnesses now call; `fgos wire-agents` still cannot install a workspace's hook rows and its help text no longer names settings the verb never writes (the survivor for a person's agent config is `packages/distribution/rust/src/agent_config.rs` with `apps/fgos/src/wiring/wire_agents.rs`). `src/setup/shell-rc.mjs` (last commit 12f8a187a) is gone: `packages/distribution/rust/src/rc_lines.rs` detects the rc files and fgOS's own `source` lines read-only, `fgos uninstall` and doctor name the profiles, and the repository session-start hook prints no shell-profile line. The mailbox behaviour addenda v7e, v7h, v7i, v7j, v7k and v7m were measured on hook bytes that no longer exist and are retired; v7n stays as its measured record, no longer compared with a rebuild, and backlog `p-irt4weqipe` owns the re-measurement. Rejected: keeping the Node table beside the Rust one (a twin; decision 2 of `docs/platform/component-authority/spec.md`). Guard: the three door rows named above in `packages/component-authority/model/doors/`.
 
